Day 40: NoSQL Mini Project – Employee Directory

Topic:
Applying MongoDB CRUD operations, queries, and aggregation in a comprehensive small-scale project to build an Employee Directory.

Learning Objectives:

• Apply MongoDB CRUD operations in a real-world project.
• Utilize query operators and filters effectively.
• Implement aggregation pipelines for data analysis.
• Understand schema design principles for NoSQL databases.

Activities / Deliverables:

• Build an Employee Directory in MongoDB.
• Perform CRUD operations on employee data.
• Use aggregation to group employees by department.
• Validate and test the functionality of the project.

Important Concepts:

• CRUD operations (insert, find, update, delete).
• Query operators ($eq, $gt, $lt, $in, $and, $or, $not).
• Aggregation stages ($match, $group, $project, $sort).
• Schema design (embedding vs referencing).

SQL Syntax / Commands:

• db.collection.insertOne()
• db.collection.find()
• db.collection.updateMany()
• db.collection.deleteOne()
• db.collection.aggregate()

Real-world Use Cases:

• Managing employee records in HR systems.
• Organizing departmental data for analysis.
• Creating dynamic employee directories for organizations.

Tools / Tech:

• MongoDB 7
• MongoDB Compass

Summary:
On Day 40, the focus was on consolidating MongoDB skills by building an Employee Directory. This project involved performing CRUD operations, using query operators, and implementing aggregation pipelines to analyze employee data by department. The activity reinforced the practical application of NoSQL concepts in real-world scenarios, enhancing proficiency in MongoDB tools and techniques.

